# The findings the image scan of .github/workflows/docker-image.yml accepts; everything not
# named here still fails it. Each entry carries the date it is due back for review: past that
# date Trivy counts the finding again and the gate goes red until someone has looked a second
# time.
#
# TinyMCE 5.10.9, the admin content editor: three stored cross-site-scripting bypasses in its
# own content parser (data-mce-* attributes, the media plugin's data-mce-object, mce:protected
# comments). They are patched in 7.9.3 and 8.5.1, and on the 5.x line in 5.11.1, which is
# published under a commercial support contract - so nothing installable closes them here,
# while Trivy reports them as fixed and ignore-unfixed therefore leaves them in. The fix is the
# editor major, which is a piece of work of its own. Until it happens, the exposure is an
# editor served to authenticated administrators and content authored through it.
# TODO: Must be refactored in Step 5.1 (Modern Block Editor) - these go with the editor they cover
